      "writtenOn": "2026-08-07T10:42:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am worried about this logic here because it is susceptible to read-modify-write. If an attacker can trigger the rollback it can then modify the content of the entry so that it will later control the donation path.\n\nExample: \n1. let\u0027s say host has an invalid entry and hyp has a valid one. Host issues a MAPD command\n2. the change in the valid bit is detected and __pkvm_hyp_donate_host is triggered\n3. the attacker triggers the rollback logic and patches the entry in the host table to make it valid again\n4. the lvl2_table remains given to the host -\u003e game over",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 259,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "dcc807047583fc5418c9571613cecd301e9b73b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e811a8b8_e69fd734",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/its_emulate.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 261,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-07T11:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(correction) : in the previous example at step 4 the table remains given to the host but it is still an invalid mapping so it shouldn\u0027t do any harm.\n\nHowever the problem arrises from a different source:\n1. Host (has entry valid)       Hyp(has entry valid)\n2. MAPD is issued from the host and a rollback is triggered\n3. new_entry will `incorrectly have the valid bit cleared on rollback` even though there was no state update because ( Host (has entry valid)       Hyp(has entry valid)).",
      "parentUuid": "d79b8aad_cb79d3b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 259,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "dcc807047583fc5418c9571613cecd301e9b73b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8cc989f_b0f07afe",
